# P08 client-visible configuration. Anything secret-shaped here fails the build (scripts/assert-env.mjs).
# The rule is not "don't commit secrets": it is "the client bundle must not be able to carry one", so the
# prefix itself is the boundary and the check greps for secret-shaped names behind that prefix.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=/api
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_ORIGIN=
# Server-side only (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix; read by the proxy route, never shipped to the browser):
#   PGM_API_ORIGIN            origin of the FastAPI planes (services/api); /api/* is a route handler that
#                             forwards to it, so there is no second destination to configure — an earlier
#                             revision of this file named PGM_PROXY_DEST, which nothing reads. A variable in
#                             an example file that no code consults is how a deployment "configures" a control
#                             it does not have.
#   PGM_ALLOWED_ORIGINS       comma-separated origins allowed to POST (cross-site proxy deployments only)
#   PGM_COOKIE_DOMAIN         omit on localhost
#   PGM_TMA_BASE_PATH         /tma when deployed as the Mini App
